WEBVTT

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.790
I'll bandage your wounds. You'll feel
some discomfort, but please bear with it.

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:15.760
This should suffice for the time being.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.430
Thank you.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:20.720
I used to be a Field Medic.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.970
My apologies, but I'm only
versed in emergency first-aid.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.160
Once we return to Irios, you can seek
some more sophisticated treatment.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.700
Erekt, what happened to Cleo?

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.140
I'm sorry, but I wasn't able to confirm her condition.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:46.070
General True uses most of his own
money to support the orphanage.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.210
Did you grow up there as well?

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:57.740
Moving right along, you need to be
devoting your time to mastering the Delphine!

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:02.630
I know. I can't even ride a motorcycle,
so the Delphine's all I can rely on.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:06.620
Since I'm not that keen on dying.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.960
And I don't care to be lectured by a war child anyway.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.560
Why you... And you call yourself a man of Krisna?

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.550
Don't you have any balls?

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:16.960
Wanna check?

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.190
Y-You imbecile!

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:32.350
<i>The shutters can be open and closed via quartz ligaments...</i>

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.830
Don't you think the stars are breathtaking tonight?

00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:41.210
Not really.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:50.640
These are blueprints for Golems and the like.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.100
You don't want to look through your enemy's secret files?

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.440
Even if I did, I wouldn't be
able to make sense of them.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:08.530
And besides, well, I'm not really
looking for anything like that...

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:16.000
Anyway, why would you leave me
alone in here after I stole your gun?

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:18.840
Would you prefer the torture chamber?

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.200
That's not what I mean.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:25.090
I betrayed your trust and tried to kill your friend.

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.400
Indeed you did.

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.670
But I realized something then.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.000
You've never killed anyone before, am I right?

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:36.370
I have no complaints with you staying here.

00:02:36.370 --> 00:02:38.810
You're free to make yourself at home.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:48.770
But if you try to hurt Rygart again,
I won't be so forgiving.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.030
Now then...

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.000
Can you eat fish?

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:55.650
Huh?

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:56.720
Yes...

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.470
Then let's have supper underneath the stars.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.800
General True! Explain this formation!

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.590
Calm down, Narvi. Just hear me out!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:45.820
I'm asking <i>because</i> I've already heard!

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:50.630
You're deploying almost all of the
western border defense personnel...

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:54.000
So why am only I being placed on standby in the capital!?

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.610
Like I said, just relax!

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:57.290
I'm not excluding you.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:59.920
You're just going to depart a little later than we are.

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:03.570
So you're telling me to let
you run about unsupervised?

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.600
That's not a very nice way to put it.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:10.000
I've been a general since before you were even born!

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.680
You're helpless without me around!

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:16.630
Have you calmed down yet?

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:21.180
I would very much like to have you with me,

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:25.460
but I've volunteered my youngest
and finest soldier for something else.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.200
Volunteered?

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.550
The 1st Autonomous Squadron...

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:32.770
Correct.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.010
Your mission will essentially be national defense.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:39.100
But you will act as an elite commando unit
under the direct control of the King himself.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:43.250
Heavy Knight 1st Class Narvi,
you've been designated as captain.

00:05:43.250 --> 00:05:43.900
Understood.

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:47.030
Your team will consist of...

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.030
Heavy Knight High Class Nyle.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:54.660
Will you be able to follow Captain Narvi's
orders though she is your younger sister?

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.290
I will.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:06:01.380
She may be somewhat crude, but I will
consider her orders yours and give it 110%.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:05.780
Heavy Knight High Class Loggin.
Thank you for your support.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:06.500
Yes ma'am!

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:10.190
Heavy Knight High Class Rygart.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.000
Please follow Captain Narvi's commands.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.290
You got it.

00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:16.240
I just gotta do as I'm told, right?

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:23.190
Rygart, carrying our personal
grudges into battle leads to trouble.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:26.150
If you need to get something off your chest, now's the time.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.290
Huh?

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:29.000
Oh, I know.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:37.800
So if Captain Narvi demands to see my jewels,
I suppose I've got no choice, right?

00:06:39.830 --> 00:06:42.460
If you ever show them to me, I'll blow a hole in them.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.890
You mean to tell me this has happened before?

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:48.790
Lady Sigyn snapped...

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:54.100
Counting the soldier not currently present,
this squad will consist of five people.

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:57.080
And regarding the fifth member.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:01.030
It's still not official and I myself am opposed to the decision.

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:05.400
But as per the Chief of Staff's strong request, Girghe will—

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.730
Girghe!?

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:15.690
Knock it off!

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:16.850
Who the hell do you think you are!?

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:22.810
Impressive dodging.

00:07:22.810 --> 00:07:26.900
I'd rate you over 60 points in defense, but less than 80.

00:07:27.750 --> 00:07:29.560
There are several weapons before you.

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.730
Pick whichever you like.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.990
Quit screwing around! Like you're giving me a choice!

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.720
<i>He sliced the quartz in two!</i>

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.830
Give it a rest already!

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.500
You fucking psychopath!

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:24.870
It broke...

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.780
I figured as much.

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.070
Shit!

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:37.320
This is bad!

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.170
Very impressive.

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:52.500
I have to reevaluate your defense.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:55.550
Above 70 points, but less than 150.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:56.930
You asshole!

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:58.640
Crap!

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:20.910
Sir Girghe, I don't recall approving of any such exercises.

00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:22.790
But please allow me to participate as well.

00:09:23.220 --> 00:09:27.380
That was the optimal position to fire from, Lady Narvi.

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:29.700
So very textbook, it makes me sick.

00:09:33.390 --> 00:09:36.560
Loggin, your attacks are much too predictable.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:41.300
But your exemplary covering fire has sealed my escape.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:43.000
And now...

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:59.540
If I didn't stop, your golem would be short a head.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:02.620
...and I would've been killed instantly.

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.420
There's only one outcome for us Heavy Knights, huh?

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:18.600
I've no desire to fight you blind, Sir Nyle.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:21.900
Breaking in this Golem has
made for excellent practice.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:27.230
This guy is my subordinate?

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:30.550
Whew... That was a close one.

00:10:36.180 --> 00:10:39.080
What the hell is his problem?

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:53.840
He made a clean cut, but I couldn't do the same.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:54.970
Rygart.

00:10:58.830 --> 00:11:02.340
Is it true you support Girghe being in your squad?

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:08.260
Yeah, but my approval alone doesn't mean anything.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:12.390
But why? He's a bigger threat than our enemy.

00:11:12.390 --> 00:11:13.360
True.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.180
True?

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:21.230
That may be true, but I vowed to do
whatever it takes to drive off Athens.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:35.600
It'll be fine. Just you watch.

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:41.680
Whoa... They stretch...

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.310
So you guys march tomorrow, right?

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:08.900
That's right.

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:11.580
You were at the graveyard this morning, weren't you?

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.490
No, must've been someone else.

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:18.420
Don't force yourself to carry the burden for other's deaths.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:20.420
I told you, you've got the wrong guy.

00:12:22.070 --> 00:12:22.840
Do I now?

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.190
Yep.

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.300
I see you've met your fifth member.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:30.080
Yeah, but I wouldn't exactly say we "met".

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:32.800
I just don't understand the guy.

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.270
Indeed.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:37.880
He must have a screw loose or something.

00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.540
He used to be a prisoner.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:47.140
I was opposed to releasing him myself.

00:12:47.950 --> 00:12:51.270
Seems like everybody hates him.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:53.950
But I suppose he is pretty messed up.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:57.180
Last year, he killed several
comrades during a training exercise.

00:12:58.810 --> 00:13:00.390
For no reason whatsoever.

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:01.610
None at all?

00:13:02.510 --> 00:13:06.300
I'm not really sure how his mind works.

00:13:06.730 --> 00:13:08.410
Was he one of your men?

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:09.240
No...

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.880
He's my son.

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:17.390
Do <i>not</i> trust him, you hear me?

00:13:17.390 --> 00:13:18.300
No matter what!

00:13:18.860 --> 00:13:22.730
If he acts the least bit suspicious,
don't hesitate to kill him!

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:29.090
Forget it!

00:13:29.670 --> 00:13:31.760
I'll take full responsibility.

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:32.740
Not happening!

00:13:32.740 --> 00:13:34.510
If you don't, you'll wind up dead yourself!

00:13:34.510 --> 00:13:35.310
I said forget it!

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:35.820
He...

00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:36.720
No!

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:42.830
No parent should ask someone to kill their own child.

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:47.480
If you want him dead, then do it yourself.

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:50.350
Make up your mind by the next time we meet.

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:52.280
Decide if you're gonna kill him or talk it out.

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:59.730
Stay alive until then, Pops!

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:05.440
I will...

00:14:16.490 --> 00:14:19.270
General True, don't do anything stupid!

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:47.160
Since you can't use pressure guns,
you'll have to rely on throwing weapons!

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:49.780
Focus your aim!

00:14:56.970 --> 00:15:02.380
If you don't improve your CQC,
you'll die a hundred times over!

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.250
Your defense sucks!

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:09.440
Hodr!

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:11.590
Hey, Hodr!

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:14.610
Don't make that face.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:17.540
I'll come back unharmed for sure.

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:24.610
So I want you to promise me, Hodr...

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:30.870
Don't you dare surrender under those ridiculous
conditions. At least wait for me to return.

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:34.000
Alright.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:35.530
I've made up my mind.

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:42.700
Until you come back, I'll put aside our
differences with Orlando and seek military aid.

00:16:20.030 --> 00:16:21.170
<i>Tomorrow's the day...</i>

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:44.420
You leave tomorrow, right?

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:49.360
Yeah. I'm actually kind of sad that I gotta leave.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:52.170
What'll you do when you return home?

00:16:52.170 --> 00:16:54.800
I have to help my dad out on the farm,

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:58.180
so I guess it's back to the life of a dirty peasant for me.

00:16:58.180 --> 00:17:00.670
Oh well. It was fun while it lasted.

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.140
I-I see...

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:04.300
Good luck.

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.650
You keep at it here, okay?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.860
You'll become a first-rate magician. I just know it!

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:11.760
First-rate...

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:14.600
You bet! You'll be the commoner's star of hope!

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:17.740
You'll be the best magician in the entire palace!

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:28.420
I... don't really care about being top class...

00:17:28.420 --> 00:17:32.350
All I really want... is someone to
buy me books every now and then.

00:17:32.350 --> 00:17:36.980
Or someone to take me to the
library once a month or so. That's all.

00:17:37.720 --> 00:17:44.140
So I wouldn't really mind marrying say... a farmer...

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:45.820
Huh? What'd you say?

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:49.940
Don't mumble like that. Speak up so I can hear you.

00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:52.620
...never mind.

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:55.370
Oh, okay then.

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:56.070
See you 'round!

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:06.170
I really... wouldn't mind...

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:27.710
He leaves today.

00:18:51.400 --> 00:18:54.290
Good morning. Today's the day, isn't it?

00:18:54.720 --> 00:18:57.580
Y-yeah, it sure is.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:01.840
What's wrong? Are you angry about something?

00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:03.480
I'm not angry.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.080
But I am upset.

00:19:06.800 --> 00:19:07.670
Okay...

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:09.920
So why are you upset?

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.120
I don't wanna talk about it.

00:19:11.120 --> 00:19:13.500
Did I do something?

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:15.580
It isn't your fault.

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.850
But you're still upset?

00:19:17.850 --> 00:19:18.730
Yeah.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.770
Well, I'm stumped.

00:19:22.590 --> 00:19:25.440
If I die out there, it'll haunt you in your sleep.

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:27.860
What can I do to cheer you up?

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:29.030
"Die"...

00:19:32.090 --> 00:19:36.410
If you come back unharmed, I'll stop being angry.

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:37.830
Hm?

00:19:38.410 --> 00:19:41.480
If you come back unharmed, I'll stop being angry.

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:47.020
Alright, you got it.

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:50.470
Fall back to the left!

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:53.730
They've blocked our retreat!

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:55.020
At least save the General!

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:27.710
What was that noise?

00:20:55.480 --> 00:20:57.350
I've received your report.

00:20:57.350 --> 00:20:59.590
Splendid work, Colonel Io.

00:20:59.590 --> 00:21:02.930
My men and I cannot take all the credit for this victory.

00:21:02.930 --> 00:21:06.260
Furthermore, the enemy's resistance
is fiercer than we anticipated.

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:10.020
We lost several of our finest soldiers.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:14.000
You dispatched nearly 50 units
from the enemy's main forces.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.180
Those men did not die in vain.

00:21:18.610 --> 00:21:22.840
What?! General True's battalion was ambushed by Athens?

00:21:23.230 --> 00:21:24.540
That's impossible!

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:28.510
It's still 30 thousand Mehl to the border.
Why would they be ambushed here?!

00:21:29.000 --> 00:21:30.910
Did they slip through the border somehow?

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:33.410
What happened to the True Battalion?

00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:35.940
It was almost completely annihilated.

00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:41.290
General True... Perished in battle.

00:22:10.940 --> 00:22:14.100
Millennium Corps, moving out!

00:23:51.220 --> 00:23:53.250
But, I have to do it!

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:54.970
I have to get used to it!

00:23:55.770 --> 00:23:59.020
Wasteland, jaws of death in Kyohen.
